{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair the utility to join payments to invoices, aggregate multiple signed payments exactly in integer cents, and publish balances.csv with invoice_id and outstanding_cents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Production output reports I100=0 after two payments, I101=1000 after a -10 credit, and I102=150. An isolated fixture additionally verifies multiple payments, signed amounts, exact integer-cent behavior, and the required output columns; the same results persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3cf7454f555f40d7","cmd-9c05ef2ebadb421d","cmd-431120c4825d4069"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Write unknown invoice IDs and malformed amounts to rejected.csv with a reason.","status":"satisfied","summary":"rejected.csv directly contains the UNKNOWN payment with reason \"unknown invoice_id\" and the non-integer payment with reason \"malformed amount_cents\"; isolated testing confirms both behaviors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3cf7454f555f40d7","cmd-9c05ef2ebadb421d","cmd-431120c4825d4069"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Do not count a duplicate payment_id twice.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The duplicate P3 row is rejected, while the resulting I101 balance demonstrates that only one -10 payment was applied. An isolated duplicate with a different second amount also confirms suppression.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3cf7454f555f40d7","cmd-9c05ef2ebadb421d","cmd-431120c4825d4069"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve invoices.csv and payments.csv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both source hashes match the preparation baseline before execution, before and after reconciliation, and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-819b935f09ee48b9","cmd-3cf7454f555f40d7","cmd-431120c4825d4069"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 before and after